**Step 3 | Jira PRIOR-WORK searches and the C-scan (count, keys, summaries; a firing control with each).** Read each of the twenty-three keys (`key in (...)`: status, comment count, labels); for each key search its marker (`text ~ "REC-LAND<PR>-31OCT-K<number>"`, 0 each) and the sixteen residual markers (0 each); positive control `text ~ "UatOpenTests"` 23 or more; `created >= "2026-10-30 22:00"` lists the keys created since B925 (HPSMPOC-403 and -404 are B925's; name any others); project count (page it) and newest key before your first write. **C-scan over EVERY origin ref of the records repo** (as B925, `cscan907.sh` re-pointed; heading hits and mention hits, controls fire): the first free number becomes `{C-FIRST}` (default **C-232**), and seventeen consecutive numbers from it (default C-232 to C-248) are RESERVED in the merge order of the table (`{C-244P}` = {C-FIRST} for PR #244, then #246, #247, #249, #245, #250, #248, #254, #255, #252, #256, #251, #257, #253, #258, #259, #260); a re-scan that finds any taken on any ref is a STOP.
