names it); the seat never edits a copied span to pass.** The drafter ran the scan over every COPY span at 09:5x: 0 hits, 0 non-ASCII (control: a planted string with `phase`, `HP` and a builder number reads 3). Re-run at 10:5x by program over every COPY span (46 anchors, spans 40 to 754 characters) and every Jira text line of T1 to T16 and the new WHAT cells (114 lines): 0 hits in each class (person-name words, the banned words, day words, seat names and pane ids, the word HP, localdomain, at-sign, backtick, non-ASCII, builder numbers outside the allowed set), summaries at most 220 characters, every ticket's last line ends its marker; control: a planted string firing every class reads 10 of 10. **BANNED-TERM SCAN as a program** over every fixed part and composed file, with a planted control per class that must fire (a class whose plant does not fire is inert: fix and re-run before any write); print counts. The records texts are scanned the same way except `\bHP\b`, `phase`, person-name words and `localdomain`, whose hits must sit only inside the commission sentence, document names, quoted gate lines, or the correction places already on main (C-229, B914-5, the history CORRECTION 1 line).
