### Landing comment (one paragraph, no newline, one per key; for a PR with two or three keys the same text with the key's own marker)
- `<LAND>` = BLUF: PR #{PR} landed on main on {MERGED-AEDT} AEDT as squash {SQUASH} ({N-PATHS} paths, +{ADD} -{DEL}; {N-COMMITS} commits became one). It changes: {WHAT}. Gated: {GATES-SENTENCE}. Not deployed: a merge is not a deploy; the Done rule (merged, gated and deployed) is at line 1904 of CLARIFICATIONS.md in the analysis repository; {MOVE-CLAUSE}. Main's ci run on the squash: {CI-<PR>}. {RES-SENTENCE} Recorded as entry {C-<PR>}. [REC-LAND{PR}-31OCT-K{KEYNUMBER}]
- `{GATES-SENTENCE}` for a single-gate PR = "round 1 of 2, go with findings (gate B9nn)"; for #252 = "round 1 of 2 no go (gate B947), round 2 of 2, the cap, go with findings (gate B962)"; for #253 = "round 1 of 2 no go (gate B953), round 2 of 2, the cap, go with findings (gate B965)"; for #251 = "round 1 of 2 no go (gate B943), round 2 of 2, the cap, go with findings and conditional on items the gate cut for load (gate B961)".
- `{RES-SENTENCE}` = "The gate's remaining items are ticketed as {KEY-Tn}." where RES names a ticket (several: "ticketed as {KEY-Ta}, {KEY-Tb} and {KEY-Tc}"); for RES none: "The gate's remaining items are recorded as rows in the analysis repository (BACKLOG B969-<n>); none is ticketed."
- `<MOVE-OFF>` = this comment moves nothing and the ticket stays open
- `<MOVE-ON>` = this ticket is moved to Done by this records step, under the test-only precedent of entries C-178 and C-186 in the same file
- For #251 the comment on HPSMPOC-403 adds the sentence "Items 2 to 6 of this ticket are built; item 1 (a concat vault name) is declined (gate B961, round 2)." and the comment on HPSMPOC-404 adds "The three stale comments are corrected by this PR (gate B943 read it)." (checked against `B961_STATUS.md` and `B933_STATUS.md` at Step 2; a difference HOLDS that sentence).
